    "long_instructions": "# Headings, Paragraphs, and Lists Reflection\r\n\r\n🤔 Take a minute to reflect on the last level where you were tasked with deciding what tags would provide the best structure for the content and answer the following questions:\r\n\r\n1. ✔️ How do you think you did according to the Rubric below and why?\r\n2. 🏁 How did you know how to complete this assessment?\r\n3. 👍🏼 What was easy about the task? / ❗ What was the most challenging? \r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n::: details [Extensive Evidence]\r\nAll content is contained in tags, uses paragraph tags, multiple sized headings, and at least one list in a logically consistent way. Comments are used to define sections of code.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n::: details [Convincing Evidence]\r\nAll content is contained in tags, uses paragraph, heading tags, and a list in a reasonable way.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n::: details [Limited Evidence]\r\nMost content is contained in tags. At least one heading tag is used.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n::: details [No Evidence]\r\nLittle or no content is contained in tags.\r\n:::\r\n",
